// EXPECT: [E012]
// EXPECT-TEXT: a required precondition is not established here
// (I.78: `i usize in 0..a.len` is a precondition like any other refinement, so a call that does
// not establish it is E012; the retired `i usize in a` reported E085.)
// P0 soundness: the `pos usize in 0..text.len` parameter invariant (0 <= pos < text.len)
// was enforced only for a known-constant array length and a known index range, so
// forwarding an UNBOUNDED index through a slice was accepted and the callee's
// check-free `text[pos]` read out of bounds (ASan: stack-buffer-overflow via
// run(buf,10) -> at(buf,10) -> text[10] on a length-3 array). Now fail-closed.
func at(text u8[], pos usize in 0..text.len) u8 { return text[pos] }
func run(t u8[], p usize) u8 { return at(t, p) }
func main() i32 { return 0 }
